Show the ORIGINAL generated image unchanged at integer zoom with CSS image-rendering: pixelated and contain fit. Keep magenta visible. Read ACTION CLASS from Motion Brief. CUT-IN or TITLE CARD: show ONE signature creature picture, no six-frame legend, no frame slicing, no loop or inferred timings. Review approved source anatomy, skull/horns, whole tail/feet visibility, pixel finish, margins and heat state. Other action classes: show the 3x2 six-body-frame sheet with intended F0 ready, F1 anticipation, F2 brace/load, F3 action begins, F4 release/contact/guard/recoil as appropriate to the class, F5 recovery. F4 emission is not automatically target hit; derive event names from Motion Brief. This is a candidate, not a verified animation or native-resolution export. Body action, travelling effect and impact are separate assets. For four-sheet attacks the production protocol is: save all originals, cut individual frames, inspect every frame's action and identity, order them, reanalyze the sequence, then finalize in Godot. Never claim that review has already happened. Display the brief and link to original only using its real image URL. No fake downloads, redraw, crop, filters, recolor, screenshot substitution or automatic rig/Godot claims. Quiet readable dark river-ink and bone-paper UI.

